    "answer": {
      "short": "$P(A\\cup B)\\in[0.8,1]$, $P(A\\cap B)\\in[0.4,0.6]$.\n\nBound the union using event containment, then use the addition rule.",
      "worked": "Since $B\\subseteq A\\cup B$ and probabilities are at most 1,\n$$0.8\\le P(A\\cup B)\\le 1.$$\nThe addition rule gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\cap B)&=0.6+0.8-P(A\\cup B)\\\\P(A\\cap B)&=1.4-P(A\\cup B).\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore,\n$$0.4\\le P(A\\cap B)\\le 0.6.$$\nThe endpoints are attainable when $A\\subseteq B$ and when $A\\cup B$ has probability 1.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
